#!/bin/sh
set -eu
umask 077
ROOT=$(CDPATH= cd -- "$(dirname -- "$0")/.." && pwd)
cd "$ROOT"
if [ "$(uname -s)" != Darwin ]; then
  printf 'Native macOS interaction test NOT RUN: this host is not macOS.\n' >&2
  exit 1
fi
cat >&2 <<'STEPS'
Native interaction checklist (a successful launch is not a passing checklist):
1. Confirm the Juice Bend window and synthetic demo sessions are readable.
2. Type a search, open a result, and scroll the transcript.
3. Select text, copy, paste into search, and compare with underlying text.
4. Check Command/Shift modifiers and committed accented/CJK/emoji text.
5. Change a filter, inspect generation/coverage, and open Blame/Why.
6. Export captured evidence; pause/resume refresh; close the window normally.
Record observed, failed, and untested interactions in docs/acceptance.md.
STEPS
exec ./scripts/run --demo "$@"
